{
  "id": "derivators",
  "title": "Derivators",
  "description": "Grothendieck's proposal in Pursuing Stacks to keep all derived categories of diagram categories at once, with restriction functors that have adjoints on both sides. Why cones in a derived category cannot be chosen functorially; localization, prederivators, Kan's formulas and the derivator axioms; homotopy exact squares; the derivator of a ring, its strongness and its stability; recognition of cocartesian squares and shifted derivators; additivity of stable derivators, with the flip of a suspension equal to -1; the canonical triangulated structure, exact functors, the Dold-Puppe sequences, and the comparison with the classical triangles of the derived category of a ring, sign included.",
